OL,3,GNEWSACare home pledges to improve after
OL,4,Apatient's choking death
OL,5,
OL,6,FA care home resident who died after
OL,7,Fchoking on a piece of ham "should have
OL,8,Fbeen supervised" during his meals, a
OL,9,Freport has concluded.
OL,11,FPhilip Quelch, 56, died at Crouched
OL,12,FFriars Residential Home in Colchester
OL,13,Fon 5 July 2025 as a result of choking
OL,14,Fon a large piece of ham during his
OL,15,Flunch.
OL,17,FQuelch lived in the home because of
OL,18,Fsafeguarding concerns and he had an
OL,19,Fin-life diagnosis of vascular dementia
OL,20,Fand neurofibromatosis.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
